Resolve node axis names from display_hints, falling back to axes order

Add GeffDisplayHint to model the optional geff/display_hints attribute (display_horizontal/vertical/depth/time), and have GeffMetadata resolve each t/x/y/z axis name by combining display_hints with the declared axes in the following order:

1. the matching display hint, which names the axis explicitly;
2. a spatial axis named `x`, `y` or `z` (case-insensitive), or one whose name ends in `_x`, `_y`, `_z` (e.g. `cell_x`);
3. the position in the `axes` list, which the spec defines as image dimension order, i.e. slowest to fastest (`z`, `y`, `x`) and therefore counted from the end;
4. the standard name (`x`, `y`, `z`) for datasets that declare no spatial axes at all.

GeffNode now reads/writes coordinates using these resolved names, and correctly omits the Z property for datasets with no third spatial axis instead of guessing "z".

