## Frente 6 — Resgate seguro de pontos + checkout

Implementa a troca de pontos por benefícios e conecta a Fidelidade ao checkout sem falsificar origem da Roleta.

### Resgate transacional
- nova tabela `loyalty_redemptions` para auditoria própria da Fidelidade;
- débito de pontos e emissão do benefício no mesmo RPC/commit;
- locks de conta/recompensa e advisory lock por idempotência;
- rejeição de saldo insuficiente, limite de resgates e programa/recompensa indisponíveis;
- retry com a mesma chave retorna exatamente o mesmo resgate, sem novo débito;
- validade e snapshot das regras no momento do resgate.

### Carteira de benefícios emitidos
- `customer_rewards` passa a identificar origem `roulette` ou `loyalty`;
- rows de Fidelidade não usam `spin_id`, `spin_result_id`, `prize_id` ou `campaign_id` falsos;
- `loyalty_redemption_id` liga o benefício de checkout ao ledger/auditoria da Fidelidade;
- consumo no checkout sincroniza o status e o pedido usado de volta ao `loyalty_redemptions`.

### Checkout
- reutiliza o `create_storefront_order_with_reward_transaction` já endurecido pela Roleta;
- preserva validação por telefone confirmado, tenant, pedido mínimo, validade e tipo de benefício;
- continua incompatível com cupom no mesmo pedido;
- mantém idempotência de criação do pedido.

### Produto grátis
- recompensa de produto grátis exige produto ativo da própria loja;
- produto com complemento obrigatório não pode ser usado;
- produto não pode ser desativado ou tornar complemento obrigatório enquanto sustenta recompensa ativa/emitida.

### APIs do cliente
- `GET /api/customer/loyalty`: saldo e catálogo ativo da loja;
- `POST /api/customer/loyalty/redeem`: resgate com identidade verificada e idempotência;
- `/api/customer/rewards` expõe a origem do benefício e metadados da Fidelidade quando aplicável.

### Testes
- regressões estruturais de tenant, RLS, saldo, locks, origem e integração;
- Commercial E2E valida: 19 pts ganhos uma única vez → resgate de 10 pts → retry sem novo débito → benefício de R$5 → pedido de R$19,90 vira R$14,90 → retry do pedido sem duplicação → saldo final 9 pts.

## Mission

Establish the Open Source/community foundation required for OFU to scale from a founder-led repository to hundreds or thousands of contributors **without weakening** canonical authority, scientific claim integrity, deterministic one-file composition, persistence/replay semantics or exact-SHA evidence discipline.

This transaction remains isolated from product convergence. It changes governance/community/legal/control-plane surfaces only; the exact PR contains **no `src/**` production changes**.

## Current exact candidate

- base: `development/v1.1-quality-exploration`
- base SHA: `ae406dbc8ac64fbd9161566ac1367bfacf2496f9`
- head: `8b0112ca4b2b05053bda1ea81e3e38c60db7f68e`
- commits: **15**
- changed files: **69**
- production `src/**` changes: **0**
- aggregate policy risk remains **R5 / constitutional-governance**

## Licensing and rights architecture

ADR-027 keeps the existing foundation and refines its boundaries:

- `GPL-3.0-only` remains the active default for the forward Open Source tree;
- GPL-compliant commercial use remains fee-free;
- optional separately negotiated commercial proprietary permissions are additive and available only where OFU actually owns/controls the required rights;
- there is no automatic revenue royalty in the Open Source license;
- accepted Open Source Core material remains permanently Open Source;
- contributors retain copyright by default;
- a PR is **not** copyright assignment and is **not** assumed commercial-relicensing permission;
- code license, commercial permissions, trademark, contributor rights and third-party/data rights remain separate layers.

### Licensing-scope refinement

`config/governance/licensing-scope.json` now makes the boundary machine-readable and fail-closed:

- default license: `GPL-3.0-only`;
- silent relicensing: **forbidden**;
- any path override requires an explicit file/directory notice, compatibility/provenance review and R5 governance;
- current explicit non-GPL overrides: **0**;
- `Apache-2.0` for future interoperability specifications/SDKs is a **candidate, not active**;
- `CC-BY-SA-4.0` for future community/user documentation is a **candidate, not active**;
- a future network-centric server may warrant `AGPL-3.0-only`, but requires a separate ADR and explicit scope;
- `GPL-3.0-only` is deliberate: future GPL versions do not become applicable silently; migration requires R5 governance, contributor-rights verification, compatibility analysis and legal review.

This refinement does **not** relicense any existing path.

### One-file licensing boundary

The canonical single HTML artifact is now explicitly treated as a licensing surface. Public release policy requires evidence connecting the artifact to exact source identity plus license/notice, third-party and embedded-data provenance closure. The precise GPL Corresponding Source strategy remains legal-review gated; build reproducibility alone is not represented as a legal conclusion.

### Contributor-rights refinement

The policy still targets a contributor-retains-copyright model with an explicit commercial-relicensing and contribution-scoped patent grant, but now also requires any future Open Source license-migration authority to be explicit. Commercial relicensing scope should remain connected to OFU/OFU-derived offerings rather than becoming an unrelated general exploitation right; operative CLA language remains pending qualified legal review.

## Machine-readable enforcement

New exact-source test:

- `npm run test:licensing-policy`
- also included in `npm run test:open-source-governance`

It fails closed on, among other things:

- change of GPL default;
- loss of the permanent Open Source Core guarantee;
- silent path relicensing;
- accidental activation of Apache/CC/AGPL candidate boundaries;
- loss of GPL-version migration governance;
- removal of one-file license/source provenance requirements;
- REUSE compliance claims without evidence;
- licensing-scope risk below R5 or loss of ownership routing.

## Provenance and REUSE direction

The project still makes **no REUSE-compliance claim**. The migration strategy is refined to avoid growing new debt while historical material is audited:

- new material first, once the activation gate is enabled;
- historical corpus backfill in parallel;
- third-party and dataset provenance remains fail-closed for shipping embedding.

## Founding-corpus provenance boundary

`config/governance/founding-corpus.json` continues to record the exact pre-community-scale seam:

- repository `VaX1989/One_File_Universe`
- commit `ae406dbc8ac64fbd9161566ac1367bfacf2496f9`
- tree `e62971a10f3f54912197bc3904ac2f64e6c525cc`
- recorded `2026-09-08`

It deliberately does **not** assert exclusive copyright ownership of every historical path or a complete commercial-relicensing chain of title. The historical IP/provenance audit remains required.

## Community governance and control plane

The existing architecture is preserved:

- 19 contribution/authority areas;
- Contributor → Trusted Contributor → Reviewer → Domain Maintainer → Core/Integration Maintainer;
- future TSC only after real independent maintainership exists;
- serial integration lease with exactly one active canonical promotion lease;
- R0–R5 risk routing;
- Contribution Units;
- scientific model cards and provenance controls;
- generated CODEOWNERS;
- exact-SHA evidence discipline;
- current maturity remains `BOOTSTRAP`, not `COMMUNITY_RESILIENT`.

## OFU 2.0 public-launch gates

The launch ledger now contains **13 blocking gates**. The added gate is:

`artifact-license-source-provenance`

It requires evidence that the published one-file artifact is tied to exact source identity and has license/notice, third-party and embedded-data provenance closure, with the Corresponding Source strategy legally reviewed before reliance.

`npm run launch:readiness -- --require-ready` must continue to fail while blocking evidence is missing.

## Exact-head evidence status

The licensing refinement advanced the candidate from `e24f734...` to `8b0112ca...`.

Fresh exact-head workflows have been triggered for `8b0112ca4b2b05053bda1ea81e3e38c60db7f68e`; at the latest read they are **queued**. No result from the prior head is being represented as certification of this new SHA.

## Operations intentionally deferred to issue #266

These still require legal review, repository administration, release evidence or real independent humans and therefore are not fabricated in source:

- final contributor agreement and authenticated acceptance registry;
- historical IP/provenance audit;
- activation of new-file SPDX/REUSE enforcement and historical backfill;
- final trademark/legal review;
- explicit licensing-steward legal entity/person;
- private vulnerability/moderation channels;
- Discussions/categories and public repository metadata;
- future OFU GitHub Organization + real area teams;
- rulesets/branch protection/required checks;
- enforced serial integration lease/merge queue;
- OpenSSF/SBOM/SLSA evidence;
- final implementation/evidence for the one-file license/source provenance gate;
- actual bus-factor reduction, TSC formation and succession testing.

## Review disposition

Keep this PR **draft**. It is an R5 governance/legal architecture transaction targeting the active development line, not `main`. Promotion requires fresh applicable exact-head checks plus explicit Project Steward review and completion of the relevant legal/provenance gates.

