## Summary

Implement a real, user-initiated Open Manuscript Studio account deletion flow suitable for the Google Play account-deletion requirement.

### Server
- add authenticated `DELETE /api/account` endpoint;
- require the current account e-mail address as an irreversible-action confirmation;
- block deletion when the account is the last OWNER of an institution or the last central OMI OWNER;
- delete Identity account data and cascading sign-in/session/profile relations;
- delete account-scoped Studio sessions, identities, integration credentials, cloud metadata/back-up indexes, review workspace access and direct-submission records;
- preserve shared scholarly review/publication history only through an anonymized disabled Studio principal, because peer-review history uses restrictive scholarly-record foreign keys;
- remove account-authored admin audit events that could retain account identifiers or IP addresses.

### Client
- add a responsive Account → Delete account danger zone in the web, desktop and mobile clients;
- show what is deleted, what is retained in anonymized scholarly history, and what remains at external OJS/OMP/cloud providers;
- require typing the account e-mail address before enabling permanent deletion;
- clear the native session token and return the user to the signed-out state after deletion;
- link to the public deletion/retention page at `https://openmanuscript.org/account-deletion`.

### Safeguards
- regression tests verify authentication/confirmation, owner-transfer protection, removal of account-scoped data and preservation of shared peer-review history only via anonymization.

A separate OMI website PR publishes the external account-deletion URL and updates the privacy policy.

## Summary

Publish the external account-deletion resource required for the Open Manuscript Studio Google Play data-safety/account-deletion flow.

- add public `/account-deletion` page identifying Open Manuscript Studio and Open Manuscript Initiative;
- explain the browser-based deletion steps so users do not need an installed app to request deletion;
- list account/profile/sign-in/integration/cloud metadata that is removed from the active OMI service;
- explain that shared scholarly review/publication history is retained only in anonymized form when necessary to preserve record integrity;
- define a maximum 30-day encrypted operational-backup rotation for pre-deletion copies;
- clarify that OJS/OMP submissions and files in external user-controlled cloud services must be managed at those destination services;
- document last-owner transfer safeguards;
- update the public Privacy Policy with the same deletion and retention rules.

The corresponding Studio PR adds the authenticated in-app/web account deletion control and backend deletion endpoint.
